First, let's assume that you have already created an instance of the AEAD-GCM cipher using a secret key and initialized it with some nonce value. Here is an example in Java using BouncyCastle library:

```java
import org.bouncycastle.crypto.BlockCipher;
import org.bouncycastle.crypto.engines.AESEngine;
import org.bouncycastle.crypto.macs.GCMAC;
import org.bouncycastle.crypto.params.*;

// Generate a random nonce
byte[] nonce = new byte[12]; // 12 bytes is a common size for nonces
new SecureRandom().nextBytes(nonce);

// Create an AEAD-GCM engine instance
KeyParameter keyParam = new KeyParameter(secretKey.getBytes()); // Replace 'secretKey' with your secret key
GCMParameter gcmParam = new GCMParameter(keyParam, nonce);
BlockCipher gcmEngine = new AESFastEngine();
GCMBlockCipher gcm = new GCMBlockCipher(gcmEngine);
gcm.init(true, gcmParam); // Init for encryption and authentication

// Update Authenticated Additional Data (AAD)
byte[] aad = "some_authenticated_data".getBytes(); // Replace with actual data
int len = aad.length;
ByteArrayOutputStream outputStream = new ByteArrayOutputStream();

// Update the cipher with AAD
int updateBytes = 0;
while (len > 0) {
    int partLen = Math.min(len, gcm.getUpdateBytes());
    gcm.updateAAD(aad, partLen);
    len -= partLen;
    aad = Arrays.copyOfRange(aad, partLen, aad.length);
    outputStream.write(gcm.doFinal(), 0, gcm.getOutputSize());
    updateBytes += partLen;
}

