 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to your existing code. Here's how you can modify it:
```matlab
% Read input image and convert to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter to reduce noise
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 0.5); % Set standard deviation to 0.5
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction on filtered image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction on filtered image
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
In this modified code, we added a new step where we define a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function and apply it to the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function before applying the Sobel edge detection. The standard deviation of the Gaussian filter can be adjusted according to the amount of noise present in the image.

